  "notes": "モテる comes from ⟦{持|も}てる→持つ：00478_motsu⟧ (to be able to hold/have), meaning \"to be held in regard\" or \"to be in demand.\" Usually written in katakana to emphasize its slang nature.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is casual/colloquial language commonly used when discussing dating and popularity.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧モテる: to be popular with (a group)\n- モテ{男|おとこ}/モテ⟦{女|おんな}→女：00559_onna⟧: a popular guy/girl\n- モテ{期|き}: a period when one is popular\n- モテたい: to want to be popular\n- ⟦{非|ひ}→非：28419_hi⟧モテ: someone who isn't popular (slang)",
